      "title": "QT: Document SCTP Graph Dialog using 2 FAMs in one struct in C++",
      "message": "QT: Document SCTP Graph Dialog using 2 FAMs in one struct in C++\n\nFlexible Array Members are not legal C++, and I'm surprised that the\ncompilers don't complain about this since it's using the \"length 1\"\napproach instead of [0] or []. They might complain at runtime after\nrecent warning changes, if I can find any samples of SCTP with gap\nreports and duplicates TSNs in the SACK headers.\n\nChange something where instead of taking the address of a singleton\nand doing some pointer arithmetic because it happened to have the\nright type as the unnamed FAM off the end that we wanted to address\n(Coverity CID 1439124 did not like this), instead find the address\nof the end of the first FAM and then cast it to a different type\nof array. (What will Coverity think of this?)\n\nThe code is still unsafe and I'm not sure it works on fuzzed data\nor even some truncated data.\n",
